{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Abolish employer National Insurance contributions",
        "additional_details": "It is currently set at \u2013 15% rate for each employee and charged to the business. We believe that if the Government are serious about increasing employment, it should let employers employ people without requiring them to pay this additional tax.\r\n \r\nWe believe it is a direct tax that employing businesses must pay on top of employees\u2019 wages. We believe we should help businesses employ more workers without penalising the business for each worker they employ. If a business is successful, it could instead pay more corporation tax, but sadly, many businesses are failing due to current tax burdens.",
        "background": "Not to be confused with Employee PAYE or Employee National Insurance contributions, we want the Government to abolish Employer National Insurance contributions as we believe it is a direct tax placed on businesses for each employed person based and on their employee\u2019s earnings.",
